---
import GitHubButton from "./GitHubButton.astro";
---

<section class="hero">
  <div class="wrap hero-grid">
    <div>
      <p class="pills">
        <span class="pill">Free and open source</span>
        <span class="pill">Self-hosted</span>
        <span class="pill pill-warn">Early</span>
      </p>
      <h1>The AI SEO agent that works from your data, not generic advice.</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        Ask a chatbot about your SEO and you get a checklist: it has never seen your Search Console.
        Jabuti's agents pull your data, analyze it with scripts they write and run, and bring back
        what to change on which page, with the evidence. On your server, and nothing ships without
        your approval.
      </p>
      <div class="ctas">
        <a class="btn btn-primary btn-lg" href="#install">Install it free</a>
        <GitHubButton label="View on GitHub" class="btn-lg" />
      </div>
      <p class="hero-note">MIT license · Docker · Bring your own Anthropic API key</p>
    </div>

    {/* Illustrative: the steps mirror the seo-example agent template; no real data or numbers. */}
    <figure class="chat" aria-label="Illustration of a conversation with a Jabuti SEO agent">
      <figcaption>
        <span class="dot"></span> blog <span class="muted">· SEO agent</span>
      </figcaption>
      <div class="chat-body">
        <p class="msg msg-user">Where are the quick wins in Search Console this month?</p>
        <div class="tool">
          <span class="tool-name">mcp__gsc__search_analytics</span>
          <span class="tool-out">last 28 days vs the 28 before → rows saved as CSV in mcp/gsc/</span>
        </div>
        <div class="tool">
          <span class="tool-name">shell</span>
          <span class="tool-out">python3 quick_wins.py</span>
        </div>
        <div class="msg msg-agent">
          <p>Recommendations, ordered by impact over effort:</p>
          <table class="rec">
            <thead>
              <tr><th>Page</th><th>Change</th><th>Evidence</th><th>Expected effect</th></tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              {[0, 1, 2].map(() => (
                <tr>
                  <td><span class="bar"></span></td>
                  <td><span class="bar"></span></td>
                  <td><span class="bar bar-s"></span></td>
                  <td><span class="bar bar-s"></span></td>
                </tr>
              ))}
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="chat-foot">Illustration. Every step is traced, with its tokens and cost.</p>
    </figure>
  </div>
</section>
